# GroCredit - Merchant Working Capital Facility

## Version 4.0 | February 2026

---

## Executive Summary

GroCredit is an algorithm-based merchant financing facility that determines creditworthiness through real-time sales performance analysis. Part of the Groway ecosystem, GroCredit integrates with Inventory Intelligence and Supply Intelligence to provide seamless working capital for merchants operating within the Merchant OS.

---

## 1. Overview

### 1.1 Purpose

GroCredit provides working capital to Groway merchants based on their actual sales performance, not traditional credit scores. This enables merchants to:

- Purchase inventory via GroSupply
- Manage cash flow during seasonal fluctuations
- Expand business operations
- Handle emergency expenses

### 1.2 Key Differentiators

| Feature | GroCredit | Traditional Lending |
|---------|-----------|-------------------|
| Credit Assessment | Algorithm-based on sales | Credit bureau score |
| Integration | Native to Merchant OS | External process |
| Approval Time | Instant to 24 hours | Days to weeks |
| Interest Rate | Repo + 5-8% p.a. | Prime + 10-20% |
| Collateral | Sales history | Physical assets |

---

## 2. Credit Scoring Algorithm

### 2.1 Multi-Factor Scoring Model

The GroCredit algorithm calculates a merchant's creditworthiness using four weighted factors:

| Factor | Weight | Data Sources |
|--------|--------|--------------|
| Sales Performance | 40% | POS transactions, revenue trends |
| Operational Consistency | 20% | Daily operations, peak performance |
| Inventory Health | 20% | Stock turnover, days of stock, GMROI |
| Supply Reliability | 20% | Supplier relationships, on-time delivery |

### 2.2 Score Calculation

```
Credit Score = (Sales × 0.40) + (Operations × 0.20) + (Inventory × 0.20) + (Supply × 0.20)

Range: 0-100
Confidence: 0-100%
```

### 2.3 Sales Performance Factors (40% Weight)

| Factor | Metric | Impact |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Monthly Revenue | Total ZAR processed | Positive if growing |
| Growth Rate | % change month-over-month | Positive if > 0% |
| Transaction Volume | Count of transactions | Higher = better |
| Consistency Score | Revenue stability % | Higher = better |

### 2.4 Inventory Health Factors (20% Weight)

| Factor | Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Stock Turnover Rate | Times per year | 8-12x optimal |
| Days of Stock | Average days supply | 30-45 days optimal |
| Dead Stock Ratio | % of unsold inventory | < 5% optimal |
| GMROI | Gross Margin Return | > 200% optimal |

### 2.5 Supply Reliability Factors (20% Weight)

| Factor | Metric | Target |
|--------|--------|--------|
| Supplier Reliability Score | On-time delivery % | > 90% optimal |
| Active Suppliers | Count of suppliers | 3+ optimal |
| Monthly Procurement Spend | ZAR via GroSupply | Higher = better |
| On-Time Delivery Rate | % received on time | > 95% optimal |

